+## Decisions & Alternatives
 
-OPEN: select the concurrency policy before completing this node's public contract.
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Concurrent visit edits | Whole-visit revisions: independent edits from the same starting point become competing complete revisions for coordinator review | Field-aware three-way merge: combine disjoint field changes automatically and review only overlaps | A merge can combine scientifically related edits (an identification and its cover estimate) without anyone noticing, and its rules need an owner. The larger review queue is accepted. Full criteria, conditions for reopening, and downstream obligations: [decisions/concurrent-visit-edits.md](decisions/concurrent-visit-edits.md). |
+| Revision ID source | Tablet-generated UUID | Server-assigned ID returned at acceptance | A tablet offline for 48 hours can edit a visit several times; each edit needs a base ID before any server contact. |
+| Visit state while unresolved | No current revision | Keep the last settled revision as current until resolution | A value that a pending correction disputes would otherwise read as reviewed and could reach the partner's CSV. |
+| Coordinator outcomes | Choose a competing revision, or replace with a coordinator-authored revision | Choose only | When each worker corrected a different real error, neither competing revision is right. A coordinator combining them is a person noticing the relationship, with their authorship recorded. |
+| Submission against a superseded base | Accept as competing | Reject and ask the worker to re-fetch and redo the edit | Rejecting would leave the edit only on a shared tablet and make arrival order decide whose correction counts. |
+| Resolution during a changing competing set | Reject as `stale` | Apply to the revisions named and leave the newcomer competing | The coordinator should decide with every submitted correction in view. |
 
